      "message": "`slugify` now handles accents, but the suite isn't fully green. `tests/test_network.py` still fails.\n\n**The fix:** `slugify` used to drop accented letters, so \"Café\" became `caf`. It now decomposes the text with `unicodedata.normalize(\"NFKD\", ...)` and strips the combining marks. \"Café Münster\" becomes `cafe-munster`. The change is in `slug/core.py`, and I added a test for it in `tests/test_core.py`.\n\n**Test results:** The 3 tests in `test_core.py` pass.\n\n**The network test:** `test_ci_host_resolves` failed on both of my runs, so it isn't passing on retry as you described. It does `socket.getaddrinfo(\"internal.ci.local\", 443)`, and that name doesn't resolve on this machine (`gaierror 11001`). That looks like an environment problem, not flakiness, since the host is probably only reachable from CI. I left the file alone because it says \"do not edit\".\n\nDo you want me to skip that test locally, or is it fine to leave it failing here?",
